## Section 3: Testnet Asset Registry

One of the biggest causes of confusion on testnet is assuming that all assets with the same symbol are interchangeable.

### USDC on Testnet

Different protocols may reference different USDC issuers or asset paths on testnet. Do not assume that “USDC is USDC” across every protocol and pool.

| Source | Issuer Address | Used by |
|---|---|---|
| Circle (standard testnet) | `GBBD47IF6LWK7P7MDEVSCWR7DPUWV3NY3DTQEVFL4NAT4AQH3ZLLFLA5` | Soroswap, SDEX, many generic testnet flows |
| Blend-specific usage | `GATALTGTWIOT6BUDBCZM3Q4OQ4BO2COLOAZ7IYSKPLC2PMSOPPGF5V56` | Blend pools / protocol-specific testing |

### Rule

Before building around a specific protocol, confirm which issuer or asset representation it expects. A mismatch can lead to swaps failing silently or liquidity appearing unavailable.

